Nabra builds on the work of others. Their code and models keep their own licences:

- transcribe.cpp (https://github.com/handy-computer/transcribe.cpp), MIT. The speech engine.
  Built from source with the small patch in vendor/patches.
- ggml (https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml), MIT. Tensor library used by transcribe.cpp.
- Cohere Transcribe Arabic 07-2026 (https://huggingface.co/CohereLabs/cohere-transcribe-arabic-07-2026),
  Apache-2.0. The speech model, downloaded by the app on first run in the GGUF build published at
  https://huggingface.co/handy-computer/cohere-transcribe-arabic-07-2026-gguf.
- Silero VAD (https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad), MIT. Finds speech in the recording.
- llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), MIT. Runs Scribe's writing model; built from
  source as the bundled helper nabra-writer.
- Gemma 4 E2B (https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/gemma-4-E2B-it-GGUF), Apache-2.0, by Google. Scribe's
  writing model, downloaded by the app when Scribe is first set up.

